assets_used = PackedStringArray("Houses_FirstAge_1_Level1", "Houses_FirstAge_1_Level2", "Houses_FirstAge_1_Level3", "Houses_FirstAge_2_Level1", "Houses_FirstAge_2_Level2", "Houses_FirstAge_2_Level3", "Houses_FirstAge_3_Level1", "Houses_FirstAge_3_Level2", "Houses_FirstAge_3_Level3", "TowerHouse_FirstAge", "Houses_SecondAge_1_Level1", "Houses_SecondAge_1_Level2", "Houses_SecondAge_1_Level3", "Houses_SecondAge_2_Level1", "Houses_SecondAge_2_Level2", "Houses_SecondAge_2_Level3", "Houses_SecondAge_3_Level1", "Houses_SecondAge_3_Level2", "Houses_SecondAge_3_Level3", "TowerHouse_SecondAge")
per_file_licensing = false
notes = "CC0 — crediting is courtesy, not compliance. Reuses the generic Quaternius CC0
license text already in-repo (same reasoning as the other two entries added alongside this
one) rather than duplicating it.

NAMING ODDITY, recorded honestly rather than silently corrected: this pack's own
License.txt (source-content/assets/Ultimate Fantasy RTS - Aug 2022.../License.txt) reads \"Ultimate
Platformer Pack by @Quaternius\" — apparently reused boilerplate from a different pack,
not this one. Doesn't change anything: the license terms (CC0 1.0 Universal) are identical
either way, and Quaternius's CC0 dedication is blanket across all their packs per
source-content/assets/ASSET_AUDIT.md's locked audit.

First use: Houses_FirstAge_1_Level1, the fixed v1 House variant (one look, one facing —
see project/assets/buildings/house/House.tscn for the selection rationale).

9 MORE ASSETS ADDED (2026-08-26, content-variety pass Task 2): the remaining 8
Houses_FirstAge_{1,2,3}_Level{1,2,3} variants plus TowerHouse_FirstAge, all imported as
House look variants (project/data/buildings/house.tres's model_scenes, 1 -> 10 entries) —
see each new .tscn's own header under project/assets/buildings/house_*/ for per-variant
measured-AABB/scale reasoning. The pack still ships walls/market stalls/docks not
evaluated here; append to assets_used as any more are imported, do NOT create a second
entry for this pack.

10 MORE ASSETS ADDED (SecondAge house batch): Houses_SecondAge_{1,2,3}_Level{1,2,3} plus
TowerHouse_SecondAge — the pack's whole SecondAge house catalogue, which had never been
imported (a `grep -rli secondage project/` returned nothing before this run). Same pack,
same artist, same palette: the Wood and Stone materials are byte-identical to the two the
shipped Houses_FirstAge_1_Level1 uses, and the tier adds Main / Walls / Wood_Light /
Stone_Light on top. The reason for importing them is detail, not variety alone — the
shipped FirstAge_1_Level1 is 404 triangles across 2 materials with no modelled door or
windows, where the SecondAge tier runs 964-5,948 triangles across 5-6 materials with
both. Wrapper scenes live at project/assets/buildings/house_secondage_*/ and
house_tower_secondage/, each with its own measured-AABB/scale header; import-tested by
project/tests/test_house_secondage_variants_import.gd. Wiring them into
project/data/buildings/house.tres's model_scenes is NOT done — that is gameplay-engineer's
step. The pack still ships walls/market stalls/docks/farms not evaluated here; append to
assets_used as any more are imported, do NOT create a second entry for this pack."
